<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sigurd Syr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1018</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sigurd Syr was a petty king of Ringerike in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> in the early eleventh century. He married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asta-gudbrandsdatter">Åsta Gudbrandsdatter</a>, mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olaf-ii-of-norway">Olaf Haraldsson</a> (Saint Olaf), and with her was father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-hardrada">Harald Hardrada</a>. He supported his stepson's bid for the Norwegian throne, and was the last independent king of Ringerike.</p></div>
